meta {
  name: List Unlinked (Missing Kind)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/clients/unlinked
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("400s without a kind", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(400);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /clients/unlinked — no `kind`

  The negative case that documents why `kind` has no default.

  The three lists return three different row shapes, so there is no answer that
  is right for a caller who did not say which one they want. Defaulting to
  `policies` would hand a client the wrong rows silently; a **400** says what is
  missing. A caller who genuinely wants "all of it at once" is asking for
  `GET /clients/unlinked/counts`.

  An unknown `kind` (`?kind=leads`) fails the same way, from the same `z.enum`.
}
